commit 5eeb6966e62b2da7b0915bf5b8c8b2e52577ec61
Author: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date:   Sat Nov 28 00:52:15 2026 -0500

    Deploy v6.2p-x pages: v59 patch list + v52 extras, routes and nav
    
    What changed
    - deploy.yml builds with .github/scripts/integrate_release.py (new) instead of the v52
      integrator. It applies Gemini's v59 patch list plus the six v52-only patches (careers,
      history & safety laws, BD/licensing, quiz 80/100, glossary 60/80, worksheets 6 /
      storyboards 7), so moving to v59 does not drop pages that are live today, and runs the
      builders of both lines. Then the manifest fix and three CSS-only UI patches from
      Gemini's 2026-11-26/27 batch.
    - Fixes found while building: v6.2v/w/x read "--apply" as their tree path, so the v56-v59
      integrators wrote them into ./--apply and their pages never existed; their layout.js edit
      put { label, href } objects into the nav arrays (SyntaxError that stops the whole site);
      their static pages called an undefined _write_landing(). integrate_release.py handles all
      three.
    - v6_routes.js: routes for midd-pharmacometrics, labeling-spl-rems, inspections-483-recalls,
      discovery-sbdd-protacs, packaging-el-dscsa, user-fees-prv, pv-faers-sentinel,
      microbiology-sterility, dmepa-med-errors (args "c"); ref_nav.js puts them in sections.
    - prepare_pages.py removes top-level "if (path === ...) return" lines in app.js.
    
    Source: Gemini drops in patches/ (v59 integrator, v6.2p-x patches, 2026-11-26 UI batch),
    Drive: 1 -- Pill by Pill / 01 Code; Claude's 2026-11-27 route fix diff
    (patches/Claude overnight 2026-11-27). Gemini's v62s_to_v62x wiring v2 patch NOT used:
    it writes M("x.js", ...) and v6Route imports `${file}.js`, so every page would load x.js.js.
    
    Checked: the deploy build steps run locally (69 patches + 4 UI, 58 builders, test_v60
    passed), prepare_pages, check_pages.py: 837 pages, 0 failures, 0 404s, 0 script or console
    errors (live had 819); all site JS parses as ES modules; YAML/Python compile; secret scan
    clean; 390 px screenshots of a new page, Explore home and a drug page.
    NOT tested: the real GitHub Actions run (watch it), a real phone, desktop layout, the look of
    the CSS patches across all pages, site/version.json (v59's version bump to "6.1" is not run).
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013Q1iTdWpUBqFsa8QCspLHb

